{"name":"Espresso Crema","hex":"#d09c43","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"espresso","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A concentrated coffee beverage brewed by forcing hot water under high pressure through finely ground coffee.","A drink that includes espresso as an ingredient."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/espresso"},{"term":"crema","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The light-colored, orangish head of foam on a cup of espresso."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A Mexican foodstuff, the Mexican version of crème fraîche or sour cream. Its fat content is usually higher than that of sour cream, and it is thinner and less sour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/crema"}],"entries":[{"title":"Espresso","blocks":[{"text":"Espresso is a concentrated form of coffee produced by forcing hot water under high pressure through finely ground coffee beans. Originating in Italy, espresso has become one of the most popular coffee-brewing methods worldwide. It is characterized by its small serving size, typically 25–30 ml, and its distinctive layers: a dark body topped with a lighter-colored foam called \"crema\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a5/Tazzina_di_caff%C3%A8_a_Ventimiglia.jpg/330px-Tazzina_di_caff%C3%A8_a_Ventimiglia.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Espresso","wikidata":"Q180289"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f3/Victoria_Arduino%2C_1922.jpg/500px-Victoria_Arduino%2C_1922.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f3/Victoria_Arduino%2C_1922.jpg/1280px-Victoria_Arduino%2C_1922.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f3/Victoria_Arduino%2C_1922.jpg/500